csv NEWS - History of user-visible changes

Version 1.1.0 (November 2025)

  * New features:
    - csv head +n: display all but the last n data rows
    - csv tail +n: start output at row n and continue to end (1-indexed)

  * These options follow POSIX tail conventions where +n means "starting
    from line n" rather than "last n lines".

Version 1.0.0 (November 2025)

  * Initial release

  * Commands:
    - csv head: display first n rows of CSV file
    - csv tail: display last n rows of CSV file
    - csv wc: count rows, columns, and bytes
    - csv cut: select fields by name

  * Features:
    - Row-aware CSV parsing (handles quoted fields with newlines)
    - Comment line support (lines starting with #)
    - Consistent -a flag to include header across all commands
    - Pipeline support (stdin/stdout)
    - GNU-style command-line options
